        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Americas</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Lakota people</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The northern Great Plains, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-hills">Black Hills</a> as the spiritual centre of their territory; earlier the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> region and the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a>; today chiefly the Pine Ridge, Rosebud, Lower Brule, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a> River and Standing Rock reservations in South Dakota, with communities in North Dakota, Nebraska, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manitoba">Manitoba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> region in the late 16th and early 17th centuries; pushed onto the Plains in the mid- to late 17th century; horses from the early 18th century; across the Missouri from about 1750 and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-hills">Black Hills</a> by the 1770s; the treaties and wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, 1825–1890; the reservation era to the present.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the seven bands of the Očhéthi Šakówiŋ, the Seven Council Fires; winter counts; the sacred buffalo calf pipe of White Buffalo Calf Woman; horse-mounted bison hunting and the camp circle; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-little-bighorn">Battle of the Little Bighorn</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitting-bull">Sitting Bull</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crazy-horse">Crazy Horse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-cloud">Red Cloud</a>; the Wounded Knee Massacre; the refusal of payment for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-hills">Black Hills</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Lakota winter counts (waníyetu wówapi) such as the Battiste Good count, and the American Horse ledger; Lakota oral tradition, as drawn on by Joseph M. Marshall III; the journals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewis-and-clark-expedition">Lewis and Clark Expedition</a>; US treaties and army reports; photographs of the Wounded Knee burial; the fieldwork of the linguist Ella Deloria.</span></div>
        </div>
